description:
## Summary

This plugin provides support for interacting with SQL databases in Nextflow scripts. It supports multiple database systems including AWS Athena, DuckDB, H2, MySQL, MariaDB, PostgreSQL, and SQLite. The plugin offers functions to query databases, execute statements, and insert data through simple Nextflow channel operations.

## Get Started

This plugin requires Nextflow `26.04.0` or later. Enable the plugin by adding the following snippet to your `nextflow.config` file:

```groovy
plugins {
    id &#x27;nf-sqldb&#x27;
}
```

Then define one or more databases under the `sql.db` configuration scope:

```groovy
sql {
    db {
        foo {
            url = &#x27;jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/demo&#x27;
            user = &#x27;my-user&#x27;
            password = &#x27;my-password&#x27;
        }
    }
}
```

## Examples

**Query a database with sqlQuery:**

```nextflow
include { sqlQuery } from &#x27;plugin/nf-sqldb&#x27;

channel.fromList(sqlQuery(db: &#x27;foo&#x27;, query: &#x27;SELECT alpha, delta FROM sample WHERE omega &gt; ?&#x27;, params: [10]))
    .view { row -&gt; &quot;${row.alpha} ${row.delta}&quot; }
```

**Insert data with sqlInsert:**

```nextflow
include { sqlInsert } from &#x27;plugin/nf-sqldb&#x27;

channel
    .of(&#x27;Hello&#x27;,&#x27;world!&#x27;)
    .map { it -&gt; tuple(it, it.size()) }
    .sqlInsert( into: &#x27;SAMPLE&#x27;, columns: &#x27;NAME, LEN&#x27;, db: &#x27;foo&#x27; )
```

**Execute statements with sqlExecute:**

```nextflow
include { sqlExecute } from &#x27;plugin/nf-sqldb&#x27;

sqlExecute(db: &#x27;foo&#x27;, statement: &#x27;CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sample_table (id INTEGER, name VARCHAR(100))&#x27;)
// [success: true, result: null]

sqlExecute(db: &#x27;foo&#x27;, statement: &#x27;INSERT INTO sample_table (id, name) VALUES (:id, :name)&#x27;, params: [id: 1, name: &#x27;alpha&#x27;])
// [success: true, result: 1]
```

